{
 "_doc": "Portable victim-pose vocabulary for KOF96 throws. Every pose a throw list gives a victim is a KOF96 game state (+ the step of that state's animation); the state map is shared by every fighter, so the same numbers work for all 29. To reuse throws with sprites from another game, map each 'posture' (+ 'angle') to a frame of that game. posture: what the body does. angle: approximate body rotation in degrees, read by eye from Terry's frames (ROM sprites face left): 0 = upright, 90 = horizontal with the head toward the side the victim faces, -90 = horizontal with the head toward its back, 180 = head down. Keys: 'state.step'. States with a one-step animation (the throw poses, 385-511) are portable as they are: one frame, same meaning for every fighter. Multi-step states (knockdowns, releases; listed in 'sequences' with Terry's posture path) have a different length and phase layout per fighter, so their 'state.step' names describe Terry's animation only. Coverage: every state any KOF96 throw list gives any of the 29 victims (111 states, 164 steps, 104 distinct frames). Same postures as tools/kof95/victim_poses.json plus 'curled'.",
 "postures": {
  "grabbed": "standing, held by the opponent",
  "bent_back": "standing, bent backwards by the hold",
  "hunched": "standing, doubled over / bent forward",
  "hit_reel": "standing, reeling from a hit",
  "launched": "airborne, knees up, just thrown or knocked up",
  "horizontal": "body level in the air",
  "falling": "diagonal on the way down, head lower than feet",
  "inverted": "upside down, head down",
  "inverted_diagonal": "upside down, tilted",
  "lying": "on the floor",
  "curled": "balled up, rolling or tumbling"
 },
